    "configuration": "The existing exact owned-backend configuration. Only the dispatch and batch entries accept an explicit trusted requestImpl; the recovery entry accepts no transport and exposes no submit/batch method.",
    "ownership": "One existing V6 payer owner; one borrowed actual ServiceCreditSqliteStore reader. The root slot and original cached native close Promise are reused. The borrowed backend is never closed by these clients.",
    "originalPaymentRead": "readOriginalPaymentCheckpoint(expectedPins): explicit powerless local DATA; independent pins required. No backend query, transport, payment, signing or authority is added.",
    "backendRead": "V6 readOriginalBackendRecoveryState(key, originalCapabilityProof, expectedCheckpointPins) requires three arguments. Existing V3/V4/V5 entries retain their two-argument behavior in source.",
    "checkpointFence": "Before the backend query, the complete original checkpoint must match the caller's independently retained pins. Its frozen binding/digests become a query-local fixed witness. After the backend query, the exact canonical checkpoint is reread and compared, in addition to existing original, funding, intent, response-observation and uncertainty fences.",
    "mutablePins": "A backend callback changing the caller's mutable pins cannot replace the first independently matched witness. This is not a new trust root inferred from a changed SQLite record.",
    "unavailability": "Missing V6 arguments are refused before the query. A checkpoint read mismatch latches the combined connection unavailable and blocks its submission capability. Independently pinned local checkpoint DATA remains readable until close; it supplies no action authority.",
    "uncertainty": "Backend cached success never erases payer intent/quarantine or establishes delivery. Lost committed replies remain unknown; the existing sequential core stops queued-next work and normal no-dispatch reopen preserves that boundary.",
    "limits": "There is no atomic transaction across the two stores. The V6 checkpoint retains its existing opaque-byte limits, exact header/hash/origin binding and authorization=NONE. Same-UID code, native APIs, component intrinsics, externally retained pins and explicit transport remain premises.",
    "noCutover": "No V5 adoption, migration, create fallback, checkpoint repair, default/CLI switch, implicit replay, payment retry, new signing path or consumed-authority reset."
  },
